What are Rigid Gas Permeable (RGP) Contact Lenses?
RGP lenses are durable medical devices constructed from silicone-based polymers that maintain their shape on the eye. Unlike soft lenses, they offer superior optical clarity for complex vision conditions like astigmatism and keratoconus while allowing 5-8 times more oxygen transmission to the cornea. Their precision optics make them particularly valuable for post-surgical applications, where they currently hold an 85% market share.
